    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0937" n="847" xml:id="pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.922/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Siam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Baker</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-20T23:00:00+07:00">August 20, 1934—11 p.m. [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">a.m.?</hi>]</date><lb/>[Received August 20—3:33
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Referring to my telegram No. 11, August 18, noon.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d748-f1"/> Conditions here are such that I suggest the Department
                    suspend treaty negotiations pending developments. Air letter follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
